// Figure 4.4 — Sequence diagram: sign-in and an authenticated request
// Eraser: New diagram > Sequence diagram, paste this code.
title Sign in and use a session

User [icon: user, color: blue]
Browser [icon: monitor, color: orange]
Middleware [icon: filter, color: gray]
Auth route [icon: lock, color: blue]
PostgreSQL [icon: database, color: green]

User > Browser: email + password
Browser > Auth route: POST /api/auth/session
activate Auth route
Auth route > PostgreSQL: find user by email
Auth route > Auth route: bcrypt compare (dummy hash if email unknown)
alt [label: wrong email, password or inactive, color: red] {
  Auth route > PostgreSQL: audit auth.login_failed
  Auth route --> Browser: 401 Invalid email or password
}
Auth route > PostgreSQL: audit auth.login
Auth route --> Browser: Set-Cookie session = HS256 JWT (HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Lax, 2 h)
deactivate Auth route

User > Browser: open /dashboard
Browser > Middleware: request with cookie
Middleware > Middleware: cookie present? (convenience redirect only)
Middleware > Auth route: forward to page / route handler
activate Auth route
Auth route > Auth route: verify JWT signature, issuer, audience, expiry
Auth route > PostgreSQL: re-read role and active flag
Auth route --> Browser: page for this role (403 / access message if not allowed)
deactivate Auth route
